{{!--
  "Take this to production" card on a solution's last step. Context:
  `solution`. layouts/solution-step.hbs includes it on the last step only,
  directly after the Production considerations section (split-after-section).
  It is marked up as an Asciidoctor section (.sect1 > h2[id]) so On this page
  lists it, and the heading carries the id the done panels
  (solution-progress.hbs and the inline copy in solution-step-actions.hbs) and
  the step rail (solution-step-rail-actions.hbs) link to.

  The whole card needs a signed-in reader. Signed out, and without the
  script, it shows only the title, one sentence on what signing in gives,
  and Sign in (data-sol-productionize-signedout), which opens the sign-in
  modal with a return to this card. Everything else is in
  data-sol-productionize-gated, which ships with the hidden attribute, and
  the script removes it once the reader is signed in, including a sign-in it
  learns after load (the kapa-session event). The prompt text is written
  only then, so a signed-out page never holds it.

  33-solution-productionize.js drives it:
  - Plan it with Ask AI opens the drawer in productionize mode, grounded on
    the agent companion at data-sol-companion-url, its core file, and the
    part files the core lists beside it. It stays hidden when the
    productionize integration is switched off, and when the core or any part
    cannot be read, the note below says the prompt still works.
  - Copy prompt and Preview prompt need the script (the prompt is built from
    the page's origin), so both ship hidden.
  - Install the Redpanda skills for Claude Code renders only when the
    playbook sets `solutions-skill-install: true` under site.keys (Antora
    camelCases it to site.keys.solutionsSkillInstall). Set it in docs-site's
    antora-playbook.yml once the redpanda-solutions skill is in a published
    plugin release. The commands
    follow the README in redpanda-data/skills. With it on, the MCP disclosure
    is titled for the other agents, because the plugin installs the server.
  - Connect the docs MCP server is static, and written here: the server URL,
    the Claude Code add, list and /mcp sign-in steps, the VS Code one-click
    link and version, and the anonymous allowance. They follow How to use
    these docs (docs-site), so check them when that page changes. Other
    clients are only on that page, so this card never keeps its own copy of
    their setup.
--}}
<section class="sect1 sol-panel sol-productionize" data-sol-productionize data-sol-companion-url="{{or solution.agentCompanion (concat '/solutions/' solution.id '/agent-companion.md')}}"{{#with @root.page.attributes.solution-verified-version}} data-sol-verified-version="{{this}}"{{/with}} aria-labelledby="take-to-production">
  <h2 id="take-to-production" class="sol-productionize-title">Take this to production</h2>
  <div class="sol-productionize-signedout" data-sol-productionize-signedout>
    <p class="sol-productionize-sub">Sign in to have Ask AI plan this design for your system, get a prompt for your coding agent, and see how to connect the docs MCP server.</p>
    <div class="sol-productionize-actions">
      <button type="button" class="sol-btn sol-btn--primary" data-sol-productionize-signin data-analytics="solution_productionize_signin">Sign in</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sol-productionize-gated" data-sol-productionize-gated hidden>
    <p class="sol-productionize-sub">Turn the reference build into a plan for your own system: your deployment, your scale, your security model.</p>
    <div class="sol-productionize-actions">
      <button type="button" class="sol-btn sol-btn--primary" data-sol-productionize-plan data-analytics="solution_productionize_start" hidden>
        <span data-sol-productionize-plan-label>Plan it with Ask AI</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="sol-btn sol-btn--ghost" data-sol-productionize-copy data-analytics="solution_productionize_copy" hidden>
        <span>Copy prompt for your coding agent</span>
      </button>
      <span class="sol-productionize-status" data-sol-productionize-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>
    <p class="sol-productionize-note" data-sol-productionize-note hidden>Ask AI can't load this solution's production guide right now. The prompt for your coding agent still works.</p>
    <details class="sol-productionize-details" data-sol-productionize-preview hidden>
      <summary>Preview prompt</summary>
      <pre class="sol-productionize-prompt" data-sol-productionize-prompt></pre>
    </details>
    {{#if @root.site.keys.solutionsSkillInstall}}
    <details class="sol-productionize-details" data-sol-productionize-skill>
      <summary>Install the Redpanda skills for Claude Code</summary>
      <div class="sol-productionize-mcp">
        <p>The Redpanda plugin adds the <code>redpanda-solutions</code> skill, which finds this solution's agent companion for you, and the docs MCP server. Run in your shell:</p>
        <pre class="sol-productionize-command"><code>claude plugin marketplace add redpanda-data/skills &amp;&amp; claude plugin install redpanda@redpanda-skills</code></pre>
        <p>Then ask Claude Code to apply this solution to your repository, or paste the prompt above.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    {{/if}}
    <details class="sol-productionize-details" data-sol-productionize-mcp>
      <summary>{{#if @root.site.keys.solutionsSkillInstall}}Using another coding agent? Connect the docs MCP server{{else}}Connect the docs MCP server{{/if}}</summary>
      <div class="sol-productionize-mcp" data-sol-mcp-block>
        <p>Connect the Redpanda docs MCP server so your agent can look up product details.<br>
        Server URL: <code>https://docs.redpanda.com/mcp</code></p>
        <p>Claude Code:</p>
        <pre class="sol-productionize-command"><code>claude mcp add --scope user --transport http redpanda https://docs.redpanda.com/mcp</code></pre>
        <p>Check it with: <code>claude mcp list</code><br>
        Sign in for a higher allowance: run <code>/mcp</code> and authenticate the <code>redpanda</code> server.</p>
        {{!-- The same install URI as Page options > Add MCP server to VS Code
              (14-markdown-dropdown.js): the server config as URI-encoded JSON. --}}
        <p>VS Code (1.102 or later, with GitHub Copilot): <a href="vscode:mcp/install?%7B%22name%22%3A%22Redpanda%20Documentation%22%2C%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.redpanda.com%2Fmcp%22%7D" data-sol-mcp-vscode>Add to VS Code</a> (one-click)</p>
        <p>Cursor, Claude Desktop, ChatGPT and other clients: see <a href="{{{relativize '/home/how-to-use-these-docs/'}}}">How to use these docs</a>.</p>
        <p>Without signing in you get 10 tool calls every 24 hours per network address.<br>
        The server answers general product questions. This solution's own production guide is the agent companion linked in the prompt.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
